      walkthrough = "**Status: Incomplete**\n\nQuest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Ruins of Shadow Haven [zone=1308]\n**Who:**\n- Aliane SteelKnuckle [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Daesorak's Badge [item=145272]\n- Overslo's Badge [item=145271]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Paludal Depths [zone=1307]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Noppta Mottun [npc=58435]\n- a shik'nar tunneler [npc=58425]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Paludal Depths (10 Points) [quest=12239]\n**Era:** | !Night of Shadows\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Oct 28 23:26:08 2022\nModified: Mon Jun 30 13:07:47 2025 | | **Night of Shadows Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this task from Aliane SteelKnuckle in Ruins of Shadow Haven at /waypoint -660, -433, -29 in the southeast part of the zone on the way to Paludal Depths. She is on the Find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Aliane SteelKnuckle'\nAliane SteelKnuckle's eyes are sunken, with dark circles lined underneath them, this woman has not seen sleep for days. 'You're an adventurer, aren't you? Oh, maybe you can help me!' She nervously fumbles in her pockets for a drawing of a man and shows it to you. 'This is my husband, Daesorak Steelknuckle. Have you seen him lately? He hasn't come home in quite some time and I have grown frantic with worry. Do you plan on exploring the [Paludal Caverns]?'\nYou say, 'I am heading into the Paludal Caverns.'\nAliane SteelKnuckle eyes glisten as she begins to tear up before speaking. 'These cursed caves, Brell can have them for all I care. I just want my husband back!' She wipes the tears forming in her eyes before continuing, 'My husband is a devoted follower of Brell. If he is still in that cave it is because he thinks his god wants him to keep digging. What is the point of it all if he isn't there for his [family]?' Her tone changes from worried to angry. 'Gods can take him if he's still digging, that's for sure!'\nYou say, 'I tell him that his family is looking for him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Miner Setback'.\nAliane SteelKnuckle says, 'Thank you adventurer. He had either be dead or rich when you find him. If it's the latter, I'll kill him myself!'\n\n---\n\nThe miners in the Paludal Caverns have seen better days. Though they have been blessed by Brell in finding a new cave in order to continue their work, it was not without hardships. The miners have lost contact with the outside world and their clans are worried about them. Aliane SteelKnuckle has requested that you look for the miners in the Paludal Caverns and find out what their story is.\n1\\. Find Daesorak SteelKnuckle 0/1 Paludal Depths\nAliane has asked you to look for Daesorak SteelKnuckle inside the Paludal Depths. Any information on his whereabouts will be greatly appreciated.\nThis step updates at /waypoint -1300, -1152, -176 near Sharvyn Oresinger which is on the find tool.\n2\\. Speak to Noppta 0/1 Paludal Depths\nNoppta is near Sharvyn Oresinger.\nYou say, 'Hail, Noppta Mottun'\nYour task 'A Miner Setback' has been updated.\nNoppta Mottun looks you in the eyes as you greet him. 'Adventurer, I find your kind to be proud, yet capable of taking care of themselves. As you can see, Daesorak and Farlol are no longer with us in the realm of the living.' His eyes brim over with tears. 'We lost some good people in the cave-ins. Brell commanded us to dig and so we did, and he blessed us with this new area of the caverns. The [price] was not worth it, I fear.'\nYou say, ' What was the price?'\nNoppta Mottun says, 'The price was many of my brethren's lives. I was unable to save any of them. We dug for what felt like centuries. We dug until our hands bled. Then we dug some more. Our reward was more caves. I would rather have my friends back. I am standing vigil here to ensure that they stay dead. As for the rest of the miners? I can't say for certain what has happened to them. I was able to find some of their badges and will return them when I leave this place. I was looking for one more [badge] before I left this gods-forsaken pit.'\nYou say, 'Who's badge are you looking for?'\nNoppta Mottun pats his pocket, 'Aye, Overslo Herslal, he was our leader. When the cave-ins first started he was the one who held the way open for others to get out to safety. It cost him his life and I have not been able to bring myself to hunt down what happened to his badge. I thought I saw one of those shik'nar with it, but their brains have all turned to mush because of the reishen spores. Your best bet would be to start culling them. Maybe one of those critters have the badge.\n3\\. Locate Overslo's badge amongst the shik`nar 0/6 Paludal Depths\n> **Quest Text:** Noppta Mottun is keeping vigil over the miners' graves. He has asked that you attemp to locate Overslo's badge somewhere within the Paludal Caverns. Hunt the Shik`nar, one of them was last seen with it.\n4\\. Slay the shik`nar tunneller and collect the badge 0/1 Paludal Depths\n/way -965, -835\n5\\. Return Overslo's Badge to Noppta 0/1 Paludal Depths\n6\\. Speak with Aliance SteelKnuckle 0/1 Ruins of Shadow Haven\n7\\. Give Aliane Daesorak's badge 0/1 Ruins of Shadow Haven\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141pp 6g 6s 7cp at Level 120\n**Submitted by:** Gidono, Veludeus",
