      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Ruins of Shadow Haven [zone=1308]\n**Who:**\n- Tarson Lonewolf [ _Shaman Guildmaster and Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Ruins of Shadow Haven (10 Points) [quest=12241]\n**Era:** | !Night of Shadows\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 6 22:17:18 2022\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This task is received at the conclusion of the previous task: Spiritual Corruption\"_\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'That is disturbing. I expect that the explosive fungal growth is caused by the spiritual corruption. I may have an inkling of the cause, but I don't want to believe it. I need some confirmation but getting it might be somewhat dangerous. Are you [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I am interested'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Power Corrupts'.\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'Great. I'll need you to kill some of the spirit-touched and animated rocks to release the spirits and get them away from whatever is consuming them. Then I'll want you to follow Commander Yaminshavraylin without letting her know you are following her.'\n\n---\n\n_Destroy spirit-touched and animated debris, rubble, and scrap._\n_Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin, but don't allow yourself to be seen._\n1\\. Kill 5 spirit-touched debris, rubble, and scrap 0/5 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n2\\. Kill 5 animated debris, rubble, and scrap 0/5 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n3\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n4\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n5\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n6\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n7\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n8\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n9\\. Follow Commander Yaminshavraylin 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\n10\\. Converse with Tarson Lonewolf 0/1 (Ruins of Shadow Haven)\nYou say, 'Hail, Tarson Lonewolf'\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'So what was the Commander [doing]?'\nYou say, 'It started simple. She wasn't doing anything weird. The Commander started fairly mundanely. She walked to the library and looked about the room as usual for someone doing a patrol.'\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'That is [normal]. Continue; I'll interrupt again when you speak about something abnormal.'\nYou say, 'Yes, it was normal. She left the library and spent a minute observing goings on from the bridge nearby. She then went to the banker and asked if anyone had been acting suspiciously. When she received a negative answer, she studied the room, then moved on. She walked around a bit, then out into the city center where the fungal creatures have taken over. Then, as she moved east towards the wall where the stone creatures are, she turned herself invisible.'\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'Invisible? Really? That's weird... By all reports she is a warrior, so she should not know how to cast spells. Did she drink a [potion]? And what did she do next?'\nYou say, 'No. She didn't drink a potion. She used some sort of magic. I can't rule out that she had an item she could activate with concentration. Once she was invisible, she moved up to the piles of rubble. She spent about five minutes at the three largest piles against the outer wall. She would look for people observing her, and after a pause, her hands glowed purple for a minute or so.'\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'You say her hands [glowed]?'\nYou say, ' Yes, they glowed purple. Once she did that at all three, she walked back. At about the same point, she cleared the invisibility and then returned to her patrol of this area. The weirdest thing of all is when she got to the door. She did absolutely nothing but stare at it. But I swear that, out of the corner of my eye, almost out of sight, the door winked at her. But, no matter how long I looked, I could not find eyes or anything like that on the door. Nothing that makes the door unusual. It's just a door. I think I'm only being paranoid and the stress of following her made me imagine things.'\nYour task 'Power Corrupts' has been updated.\nCommander Yaminshavraylin is acting suspiciously, and something is very odd about the door.\nYou receive 5 copper .\nYou receive 2 silver .\nYou receive 6 gold .\nYou receive 265 platinum .\nYou have gained 1 mercenary ability point(s)! You now have 16 mercenary ability point(s).\nYou have gained 36 ability point(s)! You now have 78 ability point(s).\nYou gain experience! (0.000%)\nTarson Lonewolf says, 'That is disturbing. I'll be sure that this is looked into, but at this point, I don't have the power to gainsay her, and I don't wish for you to harm her. I would instead like for you to see Animist Khalan. Tell him about the door.'\nYou have gained 18 ability point(s)! You now have 96 ability point(s).\nYou have gained 1 mercenary ability point(s)! You now have 17 mercenary ability point(s).\nYou gain experience! (0.412%)\nYou have completed achievement: Partisan of Ruins of Shadow Haven\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n256 platinum 6 gold 2 silver 5 copper\nYou gain experience!\n**Submitted by:** Cylius & Laurana",
